{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on ff93a691: hosted cards selection.\n\nAccepted as landed in bcf88654 and approved in d60de8a5. On first\nstartup the service makes one bounded native query of active\ninstallations. Exactly one active declared installation, with matching\nsiblings, package IDs, definition, trusted publisher and immutable\nbytes, selects card tools. Missing, incomplete or multiple rows select\nnone. Each card read rechecks the installation. The selection lasts for\nthe process or object lifetime, and a restart selects again. Hosts that\ndo not declare UI get no _meta.ui, as 288d5988 asked.\n\nA later change can refresh the selection without a restart. File it if\nO4's live runs show that a room changes its installed application\nwhile a host stays connected.\n\nBuilder: please ratify this report by its own ID so the request closes.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}